\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For injective holomorphic maps f from the unit disk into the unit disk, let $\beta _f(-1)=\limsup _{r->1}$ $\log (integral_0^{2\pi }$ |f'(r exp(i $\theta ))|^{-1}$ dtheta)/log(1/(1-r)), and let $B_b(-1)$ be the supremum of $\beta _f(-1)$ over that class. Is $B_b(-1)=1/4$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For injective holomorphic maps f from the unit disk into the unit disk, let $\beta _f(-1)=\limsup _{r->1}$ $\log (integral_0^{2\pi }$ |f'(r exp(i $\theta ))|^{-1}$ dtheta)/log(1/(1-r)), and let $B_b(-1)$ be the supremum of $\beta _f(-1)$ over that class. Is $B_b(-1)=1/4$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.07200}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-strict-inverse-first-power-bound-for-univalent-functions-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

